      "details": "Digital, stationary sound bursts and nominal order combinations only. The touch side and lead are annotations; there is no tactile output, independent masker, fixation-light hardware or response scoring. Auditory onset is scheduled from an implicit fixation at the row start. The toolkit SOA control measures a nonnegative delay from sound onset. Touch-first timing remains a planned value."
    },
    "implementation_gaps": [
      "The trial scheduler requires independent auditory and tactile triggers for signed temporal orders plus light feedback. This profile schedules only the auditory member of each pair.",
      "Speaker and tactile calibration must verify delivered intensity and acoustic-to-skin onset. Original waveform bytes and measured timing are unavailable.",
      "The original hand-held choice pad, fixation feedback and two-site electrical stimulator are required for response capture and tactile delivery. The reported voltage is a source record and cannot establish delivered current or calibration."
